CheckTransfer_Captable_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the caller is not the class's token
│   └── it should revert with OnlyModule
├── when the amount would dip into the sender's locked shares
│   └── it should revert with SharesLocked
├── when the amount is more than the sender's balance
│   └── it should revert with SharesLocked and never panic
├── given the sender has no grant
│   └── it should go on to the rule with nothing locked
├── when the rule is DenyAll
│   └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
├── when the rule is AllowAll
│   └── it should allow it
├── when the rule is ToClassShareholders
│   ├── when the receiver already holds this class
│   │   └── it should allow it
│   └── when the receiver does not
│       └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
├── when the rule is ToAnyShareholder
│   ├── when the receiver holds any class
│   │   └── it should allow it
│   └── when the receiver holds none
│       └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
└── when the rule is Custom
    ├── when the rule contract returns true
    │   └── it should allow it
    ├── when the rule contract returns false
    │   └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
    ├── when the rule contract reverts
    │   └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
    ├── when the rule contract returns malformed data
    │   └── it should revert with TransferNotAllowed
    └── when the rule contract burns all the gas it is given
        └── it should stop it at the gas cap and revert with TransferNotAllowed
